{
  "slug": "freshprobe",
  "name": "Freshprobe",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Data freshness and endpoint liveness verification for AI agents. Probes external APIs and endpoints before agents act on their data, returning deterministic FRESH/STALE/UNKNOWN verdicts\nwith confidence scores. Analyzes HTTP cache headers, measures latency percentiles (P50/P95/P99), fingerprints content for change detection, checks TLS certificate health, and evaluates\nagainst configurable freshness policies. Exposes three MCP tools (freshprobe_check, freshprobe_batch, freshprobe_policy) and includes a built-in skill and agent for contextual\ntriggering. NIST AI RMF aligned. Single Go binary, MIT licensed.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **1 agent** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `freshprobe-check` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"check if an API is fresh\", \"verify endpoint…)\n- **Agents** (1): `freshprobe-verifier` (This agent should be used when the user asks to \"verify data freshness\", \"check if an API is…)\n- **MCP servers** (1): `freshprobe`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install freshprobe@claude-community` from `Sudhan30/freshprobe`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "agent": 1,
    "mcp": 1
  },
